    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Reply to Zophar"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job answered:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "No doubt you are the people,",
          "and wisdom will die with you!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But I also have a mind like you;",
          "I am not inferior to you.",
          "Who doesn’t know the things you are talking about? ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am a laughingstock to my friends,",
          "by calling on God, who answers me.",
          "The righteous and blameless man is a laughingstock."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The one who is at ease holds calamity in contempt",
          "and thinks it is prepared for those whose feet are slipping."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The tents of robbers are safe,",
          "and those who trouble God are secure;",
          "God holds them in his hands. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But ask the animals, and they will instruct you;",
          "ask the birds of the sky, and they will tell you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Or speak to the earth, and it will instruct you;",
          "let the fish of the sea inform you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Which of all these does not know",
          "that the hand of the Lord has done this?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The life of every living thing is in his hand,",
          "as well as the breath of all humanity."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Doesn’t the ear test words",
          "as the palate tastes food?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wisdom is found with the elderly,",
          "and understanding comes with long life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wisdom and strength belong to God;",
          "counsel and understanding are his."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Whatever he tears down cannot be rebuilt;",
          "whoever he imprisons cannot be released."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When he withholds water, everything dries up,",
          "and when he releases it, it destroys the land."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "True wisdom and power belong to him.",
          "The deceived and the deceiver are his."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He leads counselors away barefoot",
          "and makes judges go mad."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He releases the bonds put on by kings",
          "and fastens a belt around their waists."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He leads priests away barefoot",
          "and overthrows established leaders."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He deprives trusted advisers of speech",
          "and takes away the elders’ good judgment."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He pours out contempt on nobles",
          "and disarms the strong."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He reveals mysteries from the darkness",
          "and brings the deepest darkness into the light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He makes nations great, then destroys them;",
          "he enlarges nations, then leads them away."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He deprives the world’s leaders of reason,",
          "and makes them wander in a trackless wasteland."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They grope around in darkness without light;",
          "he makes them stagger like a drunkard."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
